  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry the file shares are slow. To narrow it down, could you tell us: 1) Is everything slow, or only file shares? Do websites and Teams feel normal? 2) Are you in the office on Wi-Fi or wired, or working from home over VPN? Shared drives are slower over VPN by design, so large files are best opened from OneDrive or SharePoint. While you reply, please try these: disconnect and reconnect the VPN if you use it, pause any large OneDrive sync or backup, move closer to the Wi-Fi access point or use a network cable, and restart your computer if it has been on for several days. Also, our records show your desktop (BL-DT-0108) is currently offline, so please make sure it is powered on and connected to the network. If the problem continues after that, reply here and we will escalate it.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (James O'Connor, Operations, Chicago, usual hours 06:00-14:00, active, no lockouts, VPN enabled). Device BL-DT-0108: Windows 11, 78% free disk (400 GB free), no warnings, but currently offline with last check-in 2026-10-11 01:00 UTC, so no live performance data is available. Sign-ins for the last 14 days are all successful with Duo push and no hosting or foreign locations. Recent pattern alternates between corporate network (M365) and residential VPN; the VPN is the likely slow path per KB-015. No evidence of a whole-office or single-share outage. Disk space is not a factor (KB-017 not needed). Next steps: confirm whether only shares are slow and whether the user is on VPN from home. Escalate per KB-015 if the whole office is affected or one specific share is slow for everyone. Device offline status should be verified once the user powers it on.",
